hwui's hardware bitmaps of the host flavor with their pixels.

The host flavor (Layoutlib's) has no hardware bitmaps, so Bitmap::allocateHardwareBitmap gives a heap bitmap in their
place, but one of the source's size only, calloc'd and never filled: every bitmap an app asked for as
Bitmap.Config.HARDWARE (Bitmap.copy, BitmapFactory, ImageDecoder and BitmapRegionDecoder, as Glide and Coil decode on
API 26 and later) drew as fully transparent. Now the heap bitmap gets the source's pixels (SkBitmap::readPixels), and
a failed read gives no bitmap, as a failed hardware upload does on Android. Its config stays ARGB_8888 (no hardware
bitmaps on the host flavor): pixel access works on it where Android's HARDWARE bitmap refuses it.
Test: first-frame-test's HARDWARE bitmap step (orange, as on Android 15).

--- a/frameworks/base/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
+++ b/frameworks/base/libs/hwui/hwui/Bitmap.cpp
@@ -150,7 +150,13 @@
 #ifdef __ANDROID__  // Layoutlib does not support hardware acceleration
     return uirenderer::HardwareBitmapUploader::allocateHardwareBitmap(bitmap);
 #else
-    return Bitmap::allocateHeapBitmap(bitmap.info());
+    // Minato: a heap bitmap with the source's pixels; the host flavor allocated one without them, so every hardware
+    // bitmap (copy(HARDWARE), BitmapFactory, ImageDecoder and BitmapRegionDecoder with Config.HARDWARE) drew nothing.
+    sk_sp<Bitmap> heap = Bitmap::allocateHeapBitmap(bitmap.info());
+    if (heap && !bitmap.readPixels(heap->info(), heap->pixels(), heap->rowBytes(), 0, 0)) {
+        return nullptr;
+    }
+    return heap;
 #endif
 }
 
